VK: a vertex input with no streams does not make the binding stride dynamic.

PipelineVK::Create adds VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VERTEX_INPUT_BINDING_STRIDE for any non-null vertexInput
(when extendedDynamicState is on). A vertex input with no streams has nothing to bind, so every draw
with such a pipeline reports that the stride was never set. Since e7d4c4f, which made the state
depend on a non-null vertexInput.

This adds the dynamic stride only when the vertex input has streams.
Measured on v190, NVIDIA, Khronos layer on: a pipeline whose vertexInput has no attributes and no
streams, drawn with CmdDraw and nothing bound, drew the image of a pipeline with a null vertexInput
and reported "[2005986124] VUID-vkCmdDraw-pStrides-04913: vkCmdDraw():
VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VERTEX_INPUT_BINDING_STRIDE state is dynamic, but the command buffer never called
vkCmdBindVertexBuffers2." With the change it is clean; D3D12 was clean before and after.

diff --git a/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp b/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
index d283392..49de6c2 100644
--- a/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
@@ -375,7 +375,7 @@ Result PipelineVK::Create(const GraphicsPipelineDesc& graphicsPipelineDesc) {
         dynamicStates[dynamicStateNum++] = VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_SCISSOR;
     }
 
-    if (vi && m_Device.GetDesc().features.extendedDynamicState)
+    if (vi && vi->streamNum && m_Device.GetDesc().features.extendedDynamicState)
         dynamicStates[dynamicStateNum++] = VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_VERTEX_INPUT_BINDING_STRIDE;
     if (rasterizationState.depthBiasEnable)
         dynamicStates[dynamicStateNum++] = VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_DEPTH_BIAS;
